Materials and methods
Model architecture and pre-training
The model was trained using the AdamW optimizer [ 18 ], with the following hyper-parameters: β 1 = 0.9 and β 2 = 0.999. We use a learning rate of 1e -4 and a batch size of 2048 for 200 000 steps ( Supplementary Fig. S2 ). The learning rate was decayed with a cosine schedule and a warm-up ratio of 0.03. We used a weight decay of 0.0001 and gradient clipping of 1.0. All experiments were run in Python v.3.8. Detailed software versions are PyTorch v .1.12.1, CUDA v .11.7, CUDNN v .8.5.0, transformers v .4.28, datasets v .2.11, and tokenizers v.0.13. The model was run on an NVIDIA DGX A100 system with 8 GPUs, each with 80 GB of memory.
